        "q": "How does Typelessity make the unit economics work on free pilots?",
        "a": "A pilot is capped at 50 submissions a month, so its marginal cost (OpenAI fees and infrastructure) is bounded. The real constraint is human attention per pilot, not compute, and setup is a self-serve wizard rather than an integration project we run. The model breaks for high-touch customers above a certain count."
